data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (ships with .NET 11), the **sync-over-async opt-in for the Azure Cosmos DB provider is removed entirely**. The configuration you used in .NET 10 — typically `CosmosOptionsExtension.EnableSyncExecution()` or the `EnableSynchronousExecution` option — no longer exists.

**All four methods will throw `InvalidOperationException` at runtime:**

| Method | Blocking call | Fix |
|--------|--------------|-----|
| `GetAll()` | `ToList()` | `await ToListAsync()` |
| `GetById()` | `First()` | `await FirstAsync()` |
| `GetCount()` | `Count()` | `await CountAsync()` |
| `Save()` | `SaveChanges()` | `await SaveChangesAsync()` |

## How to fix

Convert to fully async:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This means callers must also go async (`async Task` all the way up). There is no workaround — the Cosmos DB provider in EF Core 11 only supports async execution paths.
